\t...\n\tpartner->altmodes = kzalloc(array_size(size_t, desc->num_altmodes), GFP_KERNEL);\n\tfor (i = 0; i < desc->num_altmodes; i++) {\n\t\tret = typec_register_altmode(port, &desc->altmodes[i], ...);\n\t}\n\tret = dev_set_name(&partner->dev, \"%s-partner-%d\", dev_name(port->dev), port->id++);\n\tif (ret) ...\n\tpartner->dev.parent = port->dev.parent;\n\tpartner->dev.bus = &typec_bus_type;\n\tpartner->dev.type = &class? \n\t...\n\ttypec_partner_plug(partner);\n\tdev_set_drvdata?\n\n\treturn 0;\n}\n\nstruct typec_partner *typec_partner_get_partner(struct typec_port *port)...\n\nint typec_partner_unregister(struct typec_partner *partner)  // hmm, named typec_unregister_partner?\n```\n\nActually, in 6.17 it's `void typec_unregister_partner(struct typec_partner *partner)`. The body is:\n\n```c\nvoid typec_unregister_partner(struct typec_partner *partner)\n{\n\tu64 modes;\n\n\ttypec_partners_put? \n\t...\n\ttypec_partner_unplug(partner);\n\tdevice_del? / device_unregister(&partner->dev)\n\t...\n}\n```\n\nAnd `typec_partner_plug`/`unplug` manipulate a \"symlink\"? Hmm.\n\nOK, here's the actual real story — I finally recall! This is a known bug fixed in 2025. The warning \"kernfs: can not remove 'typec', no directory\"... no wait — the name 'typec'! Let me think about who calls `kernfs_remove_by_name_ns` with the name \"typec\".\n\n`kernfs_remove_by_name_ns` is used in `__sysfs`... hmm. In the typec core, is there `kernfs_remove_by_name_ns(dev_kobj(&partner->dev), \"typec\")`? Searching my memory: does a port's device have a \"typec\" attribute directory? Hmm: `drivers/usb/typec/tcpm.c` has `static umode_t typec_port_show...`...\n\nOh! I remember. It's `kobj`'s \"attributes\" subdirectory. `struct typec_partner` has `dev.kobj` with an attribute group? No.\n\nA different approach: let me search the tree for `kernfs_remove_by_name_ns` per candidate file in the typec directory. In this 7.x tree it's: class.c, bus.c, pd.c, port-mapper.c, retimer.c, mode_selection.c, mux.c, t