{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"I see, the structure of typec_unregister_partner in this 7.x tree is as follows:\n\n```\n1174 void typec_unregister_partner(struct typec_partner *partner)\n1175 {\n1176      struct typec_port *port = ...?\n...\n1183    mutex_lock(&port->partner_link_lock);\n1185    typec_partner_unlink_device(partner, port->usb2_dev);\n...\n1189    typec_partner_unlink_device(partner, port->usb3_dev);\n...\n1193    device_unregister(&partner->dev);\n1194    mutex_unlock(&port->partner_link_lock);\n1195 }\n1196 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(typec_unregister_partner);\n```\n\nSo in this tree, unlink happens while holding port->partner_link_lock, before device_unregister. Whether the actual WARN is fixed in this tree or not... The WARN occurs in typec_partner_unlink_device, when the parent directory of &dev->kobj doesn't exist (the USB device has already been removed) — sysfs_remove_link(&dev->kobj, \"typec\") → kernfs_remove_by_name_ns → WARN.\n\nHold on. I should reconsider: maybe the \"typec\" symlink feature + link_device itself is from the 6.17 era! Because the user's 6.17 OEM kernel is throwing this warning. If the \"typec\" symlink to the USB device didn't exist in 6.17, the warning couldn't have occurred. So 6.17 did have typec_partner_register with the symlink. So when was typec_partner_link_device added?\n\nI think the timeline is like this:\n- 2024 (6.14-6.16): Heikki's \"typec: Add partner/plug sysfs links\"?\nHmm... Actually, I do remember that in 6.17's drivers/usb/typec/tcpm.c there was the following code:\n\n```c\nstatic void typec_partner_link_usb2(struct typec_partner *partner)  ?\n```\n\nHonestly, I can't remember. But the question says \"determine whether an existing fix is already in this tree, or whether it's upstream\" — so: this tree = the fix reference tree. Evidence to collect:\n1. Does typec_partner_unlink_device guard against the case where dev is not registered? (Check lines 909-915.)\n2. Does typec_set_usb2/3_dev clear port->usb2_dev when the USB device is disconnected? (Where is port->usb2_dev set/cleared? \"ucsi?\" no — who calls it? Grep the whole tree for usb2_dev. tcpm.c? ucsi? Let me try grepping usb2_dev in class.c, port.h, and ucsi/ucsi.c.)\n3. In the ucsi side: is it holding the USB device pointer itself and attaching it? (The attach/deattach callbacks: partner->attach = desc->attach; partner->deattach = desc->deattach — is this a NEW field in this tree? \"attach\"/\"deattach\" inside typec_partner_desc! In 6.17 typec_partner_desc was: cc, polarity, is_rtd, pwr_role, data_role, num_altmodes, altmodes... there was no attach callback. So this tree has an extended desc.)\n\nSo who in 6.17 was setting port->usb2_dev? Grep the whole tree for setters of usb2_dev:"}}
