{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"With this, I can accurately reconstruct the code of the current tree in class.c:\n\n**typec_register_partner** (1106–1166):\n```c\nstruct typec_partner *typec_register_partner(struct typec_port *port, struct typec_partner_desc *desc)\n{\n\tstruct typec_partner *partner;\n\tu32 usb_capability = 0;  // etc.\n\tint ret;\n\n\tpartner = kzalloc_obj(*partner);      // 1112\n\tif (!partner)\n\t\treturn ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);\n\n\tida_init(&partner->mode_ids);           // 1116\n\tpartner->usb_pd = desc->usb_pd;        // 1117\n\tpartner->accessory = desc->accessory;  // 1118\n\tpartner->num_altmodes = -1;            // 1119\n\tpartner->usb_capability = desc->usb_capability;  // 1120\n\tpartner->pd_revision = desc->pd_revision;        // 1121\n\tpartner->svdm_version = port->cap->svdm_version; // 1122\n\tpartner->attach = desc->attach;                // 1123\n\tpartner->deattach = desc->deattach;            // 1124\n\t...\n\tpartner->dev.groups = usb_pd_id_groups; // 1131\n\tpartner->identity = desc->identity;     // 1132\n\t...\n\tpartner->dev.class = &typec_class;      // 1135\n\tpartner->dev.parent = &port->dev;       // 1136\n\tpartner->dev.type = &typec_partner_dev_type;  // 1137\n\tdev_set_name(&partner->dev, \"%s-partner\", dev_name(&port->dev));  // 1138\n\tif (port->usb2_dev) {            // 1140\n\t\tpartner->usb_capability |= USB_CAPABILITY_USB2;  // 1141\n\t\tpartner->usb_mode = USB_MODE_USB2;               // 1142\n\t}\n\tif (port->usb3_dev) {            // 1144\n\t\tpartner->usb_capability |= USB_CAPABILITY_USB2 | USB_CAPABILITY_USB3; ...\n\t}\n\tmutex_lock(&port->partner_link_lock);    // 1149\n\tret = device_register(&partner->dev);  // 1150\n\tif (ret) {\n\t\tdev_err(&port->dev, \"failed to register partner (%d)\\n\", ret);  // 1152\n\t\tmutex_unlock(&port->partner_link_lock);  // 1153\n\t\tput_device(&partner->dev);    // 1154\n\t\treturn ERR_PTR(ret);\n\t}\n\tif (port->usb2_dev)                        // 1158\n\t\ttypec_partner_link_device(partner, port->usb2_dev);   // 1159\n\tif (port->usb3_dev)                        // 1160\n\t\ttypec_partner_link_device(partner, port->usb3_dev);   // 1161\n\tmutex_unlock(&port->partner_link_lock);    // 1162\n\treturn partner;\n}\n```\n\n**typec_unregister_partner** (1174–1196):\n```c\nvoid typec_unregister_partner(struct typec_partner *partner)\n{\n\tstruct typec_port *port;\n\n\tif (!partner)\n\t\treturn;\n\tport = to_typec_port(partner->dev.parent);     // 1181\n\n\tmutex_lock(&port->partner_link_lock);           // 1183\n\tif (port->usb2_dev) {                          // 1184\n\t\ttypec_partner_unlink_device(partner, port->usb2_dev);  // 1185\n\t\tport->usb2_dev = NULL;                    // 1186\n\t}\n\tif (port->usb3_dev) {                          // 1188\n\t\ttypec_partner_unlink_device(partner, port->usb3_dev);  // 1189\n\t\tport->usb3_dev = NULL;                    // 1190\n\t}\n\tdevice_unregister(&partner->dev);             // 1193\n\tmutex_unlock(&port->partner_link_lock);       // 1194\n}\n```\n\n**typec_partner_link_device** (888–approx 904):\n```c\nstatic void typec_partner_link_device(struct typec_partner *partner, struct device *dev)\n{\n\tint ret;\n\n\tret = sysfs_create_link(&dev->kobj, &partner->dev.kobj, \"typec\");   // 892\n\tif (ret) {\n\t\tdev_warn(&partner->dev, ...);   // 893-895?\n\t\treturn;        // hmm, then 896 wouldn't be executed on error\n\t}\n\tret = sysfs_create_link(&partner->dev.kobj, &dev->kobj, dev_name(dev));  // 896\n\tif (ret) {\n\t\tsysfs_remove_link(&dev->kobj, \"typec\");   // 898\n\t\tdev_warn(...);\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n\tif (partner->attach)\n\t\tpartner->attach(partner, dev);    // 902-903\n}\n```\nWait — but partner->attach (ucsi or core?) — attach here is desc->attach, and the signature is void (partner, dev), called from inside the LINK operation… and typec_partner_attach (the con-level one, @2146) uses port->partner_link_lock and sets usb2_dev — this is a *con* callback (port->con.attach), which is probably called from the USB core when a new USB device is enumerated on that port. But I couldn't find any caller of typec_attach at all… The USB core 7.x: in 7.x, the \"USB core\" might no longer be in drivers/usb/core, and could have been moved to drivers/usb/? Let me check \"drivers/usb/Makefile\"."}}
