{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Discovery: **port-mapper.c** — this is the component master! `component_master_add_with_match(&con->dev, &typec_aggregate_ops, arg.match)`, where con->dev = the typec connector's device has its own kobj. In other words, the typec connector is an independent device (con->dev) — therefore \"struct typec_port *port = container_of(con, ...)\" — the typec_port has an embedded `con` that has `dev`. And the \"typec connector\" device in sysfs: for example, /sys/class/typec/typec0-... hmm, whatever.\n\nThe complete loop in this 7.x tree:\n1. typec_register_port (class.c ~2746: mutex_init(&port->partner_link_lock)) → port-mapper.c: component_master_add_with_match(&con->dev, ...) → when the USB port device (component) is ready, connector_bind (port.c) executes → symlink + (if a child device exists) typec_attach.\n2. USB enumeration: hub.c:2722 typec_attach → class.c typec_partner_attach: under the lock, sets usb2/3_dev and the partner \"typec\" symlink.\n3. USB disconnection: hub.c:2363 typec_deattach → class.c typec_partner_deattach: under the lock, unlink + clear pointer — before device_del (hub.c:2376).\n4. Type-C partner removal (ucsi work): typec_unregister_partner (class.c:1174-1196): under the same lock, unlink (guarded by the pointer) + device_unregister.\n\nAll unlink operations for 'typec' execute while the USB device's kobj is guaranteed to be alive and serialized → the 6.17 WARN is structurally impossible (as long as all paths go through hub.c).\n\nAlso, the reason \"typec_connector\" has its own dev: in class.c, \"struct typec_connector con\" has its own kobject (con->dev). The connector's device name is… let me check \"dev_set_name(&port->con\" in class.c:"}}
